{"id":"mahabharata-8-048","work":"mahabharata","part":8,"partName":"कर्णपर्व","partNameEn":"Karna Parva","unit":48,"title":"अष्टचत्वारिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 48 · Krishna on the vow and the truth","summary":{"en":"Krishna rebukes Arjuna for his wrath and tells him that vows and truth are subtle, citing the story of Kausika and the robbers to show that the highest dharma is mercy to all beings. He warns that harshness to an elder is deadly in itself.","kn":"ಅರ್ಜುನನ ಕೋಪವನ್ನು ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಖಂಡಿಸಿ ಪ್ರತಿಜ್ಞೆ ಮತ್ತು ಸತ್ಯ ಸೂಕ್ಷ್ಮವೆಂದು ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕೌಶಿಕ ಮತ್ತು ಕಳ್ಳರ ಕಥೆಯಿಂದ ಎಲ್ಲ ಜೀವಿಗಳ ಮೇಲಿನ ದಯೆಯೇ ಪರಮ ಧರ್ಮವೆಂದು ತೋರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಹಿರಿಯರೊಡನೆ ಕಠಿಣತೆಯೇ ಮರಣಸಮಾನವೆಂದು ಎಚ್ಚರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"कृष्ण अर्जुन के क्रोध को फटकारते हैं और कहते हैं कि प्रतिज्ञा और सत्य सूक्ष्म हैं, कौशिक और डाकुओं की कथा से दिखाते हैं कि परम धर्म सब प्राणियों पर दया है। वे चेताते हैं कि बड़ों के प्रति कठोरता स्वयं मृत्यु-तुल्य है।","te":"అర్జునుని కోపాన్ని కృష్ణుడు నిందించి ప్రతిజ్ఞ, సత్యం సూక్ష్మమైనవని చెబుతాడు; కౌశికుడు, దొంగల కథతో అన్ని జీవులపై దయే పరమ ధర్మమని చూపుతాడు. పెద్దలతో కఠినత్వం మరణంతో సమానమని హెచ్చరిస్తాడు.","ta":"அர்ஜுனனின் சினத்தைக் கண்ணன் கடிந்து சபதமும் சத்தியமும் நுட்பமானவை என்கிறார்; கௌசிகனும் கள்வரும் பற்றிய கதையால் எல்லா உயிர்களிடமும் இரக்கமே உயர்ந்த தர்மம் என்று காட்டுகிறார். பெரியோரிடம் கடுமை மரணத்துக்கு நிகர் என்று எச்சரிக்கிறார்.","ml":"കോപത്തിന്റെ പേരിൽ കൃഷ്ണൻ അർജുനനെ ശാസിക്കുന്നു; പ്രതിജ്ഞയും സത്യവും സൂക്ഷ്മമായ കാര്യങ്ങളാണെന്ന് പറയുന്നു. കൗശികന്റെയും കള്ളന്മാരുടെയും കഥ ഉദ്ധരിച്ച്, എല്ലാ ജീവജാലങ്ങളോടുമുള്ള ദയയാണ് പരമധർമ്മമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം കാണിക്കുന്നു. മുതിർന്നവരോടുള്ള കാഠിന്യം തന്നെ മരണകാരണമാണെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം മുന്നറിയിപ്പ് നൽകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 8.48; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 29 2019","sections":[{"title":"कर्णपर्व","titleEn":"Karna Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"श्रुत्वा कर्णं कल्यमुदारवीर्यं\nक्रुद्धः पार्थः फल्गुनस्यामितौजाः ।\nधनंजयं वाक्यमुवाच चेदं\nयुधिष्ठिरः कर्णशराभितप्तः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that Karna, of noble valor, was still unhurt, Yudhishthira, angry and tormented by Karna's arrows, spoke these words to Dhananjaya, Arjuna, whose might is boundless."}},{"n":2,"text":"इदं यदि द्वैतवने ह्यवक्ष्यः\nकर्णं योद्धुं न प्रसहे नृपेति ।\nवयं तदा प्राप्तकालानि सर्वे\nवृत्तान्युपैष्याम तदैव पार्थ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If you had said this in the Dvaita forest, 'King, I cannot fight Karna,' then we would all have known what the time required and acted accordingly, Partha."}},{"n":3,"text":"मयि प्रतिश्रुत्य वधं हि तस्य\nबलस्य चाप्तस्य तथैव वीर ।\nआनीय नः शत्रुमध्यं स कस्मा-\nत्समुत्क्षिप्य स्थण्डिले प्रत्यपिंष्ठाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You promised me his death and that of his strong, trusted army; why then did you bring us into the midst of the enemy, lift us up and dash us on bare ground?"}},{"n":4,"text":"अन्वाशिष्म वयमर्जुन त्वयि\nयियासवो बहु कल्याणमिष्टम् ।\nतन्नः सर्वं विफलं राजपुत्र\nफलार्थिनां निचुल इवातिपुष्पः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We, Arjuna, set out hoping for much good from you. All that is useless to us, prince, like a nichula tree thick with flowers to those who want fruit."}},{"n":5,"text":"प्रच्छादितं बडिशमिवामिषेण\nप्रच्छादितो गवय इवापवाचा ।\nअनर्थकं मे दर्शितवानसि त्वं\nराज्यार्थिनो राज्यरूपं विनाशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You showed me, in my longing for a kingdom, only ruin disguised as a kingdom, like a hook hidden under bait, like a gavaya lured by a false call."}},{"n":6,"text":"यत्तत्पृथां वागुवाचान्तरिक्षे\nसप्ताहजाते त्वयि मन्दबुद्धौ ।\nजातः पुत्रो वासवविक्रमोऽयं\nसर्वाञ्शूराञ्शात्रवाञ्जेष्यतीति ॥","meaning":{"en":"When you were born, a seven-day-old dull-witted child, a voice in the sky said to Pritha: 'This son born to you has Indra's prowess; he will conquer all brave enemies."}},{"n":7,"text":"अयं जेता खाण्डवे देवसंघा-\nन्सर्वाणि भूतान्यपि चोत्तमौजाः ।\nअयं जेता मद्रकलिङ्गकेकया-\nनयं कुरून्हन्ति च राजमध्ये ॥","meaning":{"en":"He will conquer the hosts of gods at Khandava, and all beings, with great strength; he will conquer the Madrakas, Kalingas and Kekayas, and he will strike down the Kurus in the midst of the kings."}},{"n":8,"text":"अस्मात्परो न भविता धनुर्धरो\nन वै भूतः कश्चन जातु जेता ।\nइच्छन्नार्यः सर्वभूतानि कुर्या-\nद्वशे वशी सर्वसमाप्तविद्यः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There will be no archer greater than he, and no one born ever conquers him. If he wished, that noble, self-controlled master of all knowledge could bring all beings under his control."}},{"n":9,"text":"कान्त्या शशाङ्कस्य जवेन वायोः\nस्थैर्येण मेरोः क्षमया पृथिव्याः ।\nसूर्यस्य भासा धनदस्य लक्ष्म्या\nशौर्येण शक्रस्य बलेन विष्णोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In beauty equal to the moon, in speed to the wind, in steadiness to Meru, in patience to the earth, in brilliance to the sun, in splendor to the lord of wealth, in valor to Indra, in strength to Vishnu,"}},{"n":10,"text":"तुल्यो महात्मा तव कुन्ति पुत्रो\nजातोऽदितेर्विष्णुरिवारिहन्ता ।\nस्वेषां जयाय द्विषतां वधाय\nख्यातोऽमितौजाः कुलतन्तुकर्ता ॥","meaning":{"en":"your great-souled son, Kunti, born like Vishnu born of Aditi, will slay his enemies. For the victory of his own and the death of foes he will be famed, of boundless energy, the one to carry on the family line.'"}},{"n":11,"text":"इत्यन्तरिक्षे शतशृङ्गमूर्ध्नि\nतपस्विनां शृण्वतां वागुवाच ।\nएवंविधं त्वां तच्च नाभूत्तवाद्य\nदेवा हि नूनमनृतं वदन्ति ॥","meaning":{"en":"That is what the voice said in the sky above the Shatashringa peak, as the ascetics listened. But it has not come true of you today; surely the gods speak untruth."}},{"n":12,"text":"तथापरेषामृषिसत्तमानां\nश्रुत्वा गिरं पूजयतां सदैव ।\nन संनतिं प्रैमि सुयोधनस्य\nन त्वा जानाम्याधिरथेर्भयार्तम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And I have always heard the words of other best of seers who honor you in the same way. I do not bow to Suyodhana, yet I never knew you to be afraid of the son of Adhiratha."}},{"n":13,"text":"त्वष्ट्रा कृतं वाहमकूजनाक्षं\nशुभं समास्थाय कपिध्वजं त्वम् ।\nखड्गं गृहीत्वा हेमचित्रं समिद्धं\nधनुश्चेदं गाण्डिवं तालमात्रम् ।\nस केशवेनोह्यमानः कथं नु\nकर्णाद्भीतो व्यपयातोऽसि पार्थ ॥","meaning":{"en":"You had the splendid monkey-banner chariot made by Tvashtri, with noiseless axles, you took up a sword bright with gold and this Gandiva bow, a palm-tree tall. Driven by Keshava, how then did you flee from Karna in fear, Partha?"}},{"n":14,"text":"धनुश्चैतत्केशवाय प्रदाय\nयन्ताभविष्यस्त्वं रणे चेद्दुरात्मन् ।\nततोऽहनिष्यत्केशवः कर्णमुग्रं\nमरुत्पतिर्वृत्रमिवात्तवज्रः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you, wicked one, had handed this bow to Keshava and become the charioteer yourself in the battle, then Keshava would have killed fierce Karna, as the lord of the Maruts, with his thunderbolt in hand, killed Vritra."}},{"n":15,"text":"मासेऽपतिष्यः पञ्चमे त्वं प्रकृच्छ्रे\nन वा गर्भोऽप्यभविष्यः पृथायाः ।\nतत्ते श्रमो राजपुत्राभविष्य-\nन्न संग्रामादपयातुं दुरात्मन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You would have fallen in the fifth month in great hardship, or Pritha would never have conceived. Then, prince, you would have been spared this toil, and, wicked one, not have run from the battle.\""}}]}]}